# Browsing contract/status/field meanings: ../docs/API-BROWSING.md
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Replace with real IDs returned by browsing/seat endpoints.
@bookingId = 123
@holdToken = REPLACE_WITH_PRIVATE_TOKEN_FROM_CREATION
//API TESTS

### 1. GET ALL FILMS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/films

### GET FILM BY ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/films/1



### GET CITIES
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities

### GET CITY BY ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/1



### GET SCREEN BY ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens/1

### GET ALL SCREENS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens



### SCREENS BY CITY (static capacities, not current availability)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens?cityId=1

### MISSING ENTITY (404 when the valid ID does not exist)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/films/2147483647

### MALFORMED DETAIL ID (400, no SQL query)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/1.5

### MALFORMED CITY FILTER (400; repeated/bracket values also rejected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens?cityId=invalid

### UNKNOWN VALID CITY FILTER (200 with an empty data array when absent)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens?cityId=2147483647

### SCREENING AVAILABILITY (screening-specific counts, no hold)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/seats/availability?screenId=1&screeningId=1

### GET SEATS FROM SCREEN ID 1 AND SCREENING ID 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/seats?screenId=1&screeningId=1

### STATIC INVENTORY ONLY (not screening occupancy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/seats?screenId=1



### GET ALL SCREENINGS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screenings

### GET SCREENINGS BY CITY id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screenings?cityId=1



### GET PRICES
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/prices




### CREATE AN UNPAID FIVE-MINUTE HOLD (201; requires configured adult price)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "screeningId": 1,
    "seatId": [12],
    "clientEmail": "test@client.com"
}

### CREATE A HOLD WITH ADULT/CHILD PRICES (child is half adult)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screeningId": 1,
  "seatId": [
    { "seatId": 12, "category": "adult" },
    { "seatId": 14, "category": "child" }
  ],
  "clientEmail": "perhe.matkustaja@example.com"
}

### GET BOOKINGS WITH SCREENING FILTER
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings?screeningId=1

### STAFF PROTOTYPE: AUTHORIZATION REMAINS #35 (not a public browsing contract)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings

### RELEASE ONLY YOUR UNPAID HOLD (history retained; missing token returns 401)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{holdToken}}


### 4. INVALID TEST MISSING seatID (returns 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screeningId": 1,
  "seatId": []
}



### SCREENINGS BY SCREEN (use IDs returned by the city/screen/film APIs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screenings?screenId=1

### SCREENINGS BY CITY, SCREEN AND FILM (filters combine with AND)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screenings?cityId=1&screenId=1&filmId=1

### INVALID SCREEN FILTER (expected 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screenings?screenId=1.5


### PREVIEW A COMPLETE SELECTION (no allocation; replace with matching real IDs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/seats/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screenId": 1,
  "screeningId": 9,
  "seatIds": [2, 3]
}

### PREVIEW MALFORMED DUPLICATE SELECTION (expected 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/seats/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screenId": 1,
  "screeningId": 9,
  "seatIds": [2, 2]
}


### RETRYABLE GUEST HOLD (same private key + same choices recovers the original active hold)
# Generate a fresh 32-byte cryptographic random base64url key outside this tracked file.
# Supply it through private REST-client environment configuration, never a public request ID.
# The key is also the hold's bearer credential. Reuse only when retrying this same request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{privateHoldRequestKey}}

{
  "screeningId": 1,
  "seatId": [12],
  "clientEmail": "customer@example.invalid"
}


### GUEST CHECKOUT QUOTE (no contact needed; creates no hold)
# Example IDs from local presentation fixtures; use current API-returned IDs.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screeningId": 25,
  "seatId": [{"seatId": 2, "category": "adult"}, {"seatId": 103, "category": "child"}]
}

### START CHECKOUT ONLY AFTER REVIEWING THE SERVER QUOTE
# Set reviewedQuoteFingerprint from the quote response and privateHoldRequestKey
# in private REST-client configuration. Reuse the exact body/key on uncertain retries.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{privateHoldRequestKey}}

{
  "screeningId": 25,
  "seatId": [{"seatId": 2, "category": "adult"}, {"seatId": 103, "category": "child"}],
  "clientEmail": "customer@example.invalid",
  "expectedQuote": "{{reviewedQuoteFingerprint}}"
}
